The Friends of Aut are people who do small favors for [[Aut]] and take small rewards for them: an introduction, a nudge, a piece of luck. They do not take Aut for a god, and most of them came to him over a favor he did them before they knew what he was.

They keep an office on the ground floor of the [[Pharos]], entered at 13 Bright Street in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]]. Its entrance hall is hung with eight or nine portraits of raimented people of different faiths, and set into the floor is a seal of black stone holding three blue gems in the shape of Aut's three-dot mark. Above the hall is a threshold room with the shelf of voice boxes and a black doorway into the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]]. Guests wait with lemon water and pastries, and are sent on with a week-old report on conditions past the threshold, which warns of shadows and tells them to keep their voice box on them.
